          "new_text": "def matrix_free_spectral_embedding(\n    counts: np.ndarray,\n    n_components: int,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Return leading spectral coordinates for a cell-by-feature count matrix.\"\"\"\n\n    # Validate inputs\n    if not np.isfinite(counts).all():\n        raise ValueError(\"Input contains non-finite values.\")\n    if (counts < 0).any():\n        raise ValueError(\"Input contains negative values.\")\n    if (counts.sum(axis=1) == 0).any():\n        raise ValueError(\"Input contains all-zero cell rows.\")\n    n_cells, n_features = counts.shape\n    if not (1 <= n_components < n_cells):\n        raise ValueError(\"n_components must be in range [1, n_cells).\")\n\n    # Define matrix-free linear operator for the Gram matrix counts @ counts.T\n    def matvec(v):\n        return counts @ (counts.T @ v)\n\n    from scipy.sparse.linalg import LinearOperator, eigsh\n\n    op = LinearOperator((n_cells, n_cells), matvec=matvec, dtype=counts.dtype)\n\n    # Set initial vector for reproducibility\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(random_state)\n    v0 = rng.rand(n_cells)\n\n    # Compute leading eigenvalues and eigenvectors\n    eigenvalues, eigenvectors = eigsh(op, k=n_components, which='LA', v0=v0)\n\n    # Sort descending by eigenvalue\n    idx = np.argsort(eigenvalues)[::-1]\n    eigenvalues = eigenvalues[idx]\n    eigenvectors = eigenvectors[:, idx]\n\n    return eigenvalues, eigenvectors"
